What does the following program print across consecutive method invocations?

```java
class TrackerService {
    void execute() {
        int invocationCount = 0;
        invocationCount++;
        System.out.print(invocationCount + " ");
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        TrackerService service = new TrackerService();
        service.execute();
        service.execute();
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following field shadowing program?

```java
class SensorDevice {
    int reading = 10;
    void update(int reading) {
        reading = reading + 5;
        System.out.print(reading + " " + this.reading);
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SensorDevice dev = new SensorDevice();
        dev.update(20);
    }
}
```

Trace variable evaluation in this class comparing field defaults with local scoping. What is output?

```java
public class Main {
    int metric;
    void evaluate() {
        int metric = 100;
        {
            int nested = metric + 5;
            System.out.print(nested + " ");
        }
        System.out.print(this.metric + " ");
        System.out.println(metric);
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Main().evaluate();
    }
}
```

Examine how default values and shadowing interact in constructor execution. What does this code print?

```java
class AccountToken {
    int balance;
    String owner;
    AccountToken(String owner) {
        System.out.print(this.balance + " " + this.owner + " ");
        this.owner = owner;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        AccountToken token = new AccountToken("Alice");
        System.out.println(token.owner);
    }
}
```

What is printed by the following accumulator program?

```java
class DataLogger {
    int sum = 0;
    void accumulate(int sum) {
        this.sum += sum;
        sum = 0;
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DataLogger logger = new DataLogger();
        logger.accumulate(15);
        logger.accumulate(25);
        System.out.println(logger.sum);
    }
}
```

